%I A393481 #20 Oct 12 2026 00:24:28
%S A393481 4285700,4496900
%N A393481 Numbers k such that sigma(k) = psi(k) + tau(k) + Omega(k)^8.
%C A393481 The sequence is complete. Put L := Omega(k). For every nonsquarefree k with L >= 5, one has sigma(k) - psi(k) - tau(k) >= 2^(L-1) - L - 2. Since solutions require this difference to equal L^8, we obtain L <= 44. Checking the remaining prime-exponent patterns leaves only k = 2^2*5^2*p*q, where p and q are distinct primes different from 2 and 5, satisfying (p+1)*(q+1) = 45396. The only admissible unordered pairs are {p,q} = {17,2521} and {193,233}, giving exactly the two listed terms. - _Max Alekseyev_, Oct 11 2026
%e A393481 4285700 is a term since sigma(4285700) = 9850932 = 8171280 + 36 + 6^8 = psi(4285700) + tau(4285700) + Omega(4285700)^8.
%o A393481 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); sigma(f) == prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) + numdiv(f) + bigomega(f)^8; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Apr 13 2026
